  "timings_method": "each variant runs 3 or 10 calls per round with one torch.mps.synchronize at the end; variants are interleaved round by round, so a load spike hits all of them; median and min over 5 or 9 rounds are recorded. speedup_overlay_vs_cpu is cpu_kernel.min / mps_overlay_offsets_cpu.min: below 1 means the overlay is slower, and the offsets_to_host entry measures the synchronization the device-offsets path adds",
  "timings_load_average": [
    7.49,
    7.49
  ],
  "notes": [
    "the structure (indices in construction order, values, nnz, coalesced flag, dtype, shape) is byte-identical to the CPU kernel on every parity case; the COO result is deliberately not coalesced when nnz > 1, matching the CPU kernel",
    "offsets on MPS cost one bulk device-to-host read because nnz and the duplicate check are data-dependent; offsets on the host cost none. Index construction is one Metal kernel and the values are one index_select, both on the GPU",
    "out-of-range offsets that still give a non-negative count add nothing, as on CPU; a diagonal row longer than the matrix produces the same out-of-bounds row indices as the CPU kernel on rectangular shapes",
    "values keep the diagonals dtype; the MPS backend has no float64, so float64 diagonals fail on the device before this overlay is reached",
    "of the layouts the operator accepts, only sparse COO can exist on MPS in 2.14.1; CSR and CSC raise NotImplementedError",
    "timing includes the Python dispatch frame and one sparse constructor call; the CPU kernel number is a scale reference for the same build, not a cross-device speed claim",
    "the overlay's per-call cost is dominated by dispatch, one Metal kernel, one index_select and the sparse constructor rather than by nnz, so it beats the CPU kernel only once nnz is large; before this overlay the operator had no MPS implementation at all",
    "the host is shared with other builds, so a round's median is inflated by contention; the minimum is the closer estimate and the interleaved ratios are the stable part of these numbers"
  ]
